# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Jaesun Kim et al. (2024). Data-Efficient Multifidelity Training for High-Fidelity Machine Learning Interatomic Potentials.
#   Journal of the American Chemical Society. doi:10.1021/jacs.4c14455  arXiv:2409.07947v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2409.07947v1 (sha256 bba1319151b4bba6...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 69 (Training/reliability). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: the multi-fidelity training scheme implemented in
# SevenNet (SevenNet-MF) and the two models whose errors the paper
# prints: the multi-fidelity model for the solid electrolyte Li6PS5Cl
# (PBE as low fidelity, SCAN as high fidelity) and the pretrained
# universal multi-fidelity model SevenNet-MF-0 (Materials Project PBE
# and r2SCAN data).

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
