###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - SevenNet-MF is encoded as an implementation of the registry method entity:NequIP; the multi-fidelity mechanism (fidelity-dependent parameters) is described in the implementation node. If multi-fidelity models must be queryable as a class, that needs a schema term.
# - Each model has a low-fidelity and a high-fidelity channel; the printed errors do not say which channel or which fidelity subset they refer to. Stress errors are in kbar (no unit individual; mlips:hasUnit omitted).
# - Not encoded: the single-fidelity comparison models for Li6PS5Cl (high-fidelity, low-fidelity, baseline), the InxGa1-xN study (PBE and r2SCAN), the molecular examples, and the property results (Li-ion conductivity and activation energies in Table 1, phase diagrams, formation-energy and volume MAEs of the universal models), which are figures or have no MetricProperty.
# - SevenNet-MF-0 is paper-local here; lysogorskiy2026 compares against a later 'SevenNet-MF-ompa', which is a different model.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).

